Heritage and Attribution
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

XSpaceWar-AI is a modern, original reimagining inspired by the classic
networked space-fighter lineage:

  * Spacewar!  - Originally created in 1962 at MIT for the DEC PDP-1 by
    Steve Russell, Martin Graetz, Wayne Wiitanen, and collaborators of the
    "Hingham Institute." Spacewar! has been released by its authors under
    the MIT License.

  * Spacewar! PDP-11 port - Ported to the DEC PDP-11 architecture by
    Bill Seiler and Larry Bryant (1974). This PDP-11 networked-fighter
    heritage is the spirit this project carries forward.

  * xspacewar (version 1.2) - An X11 networked version written in C by
    Ron Frederick in 1992, one of the early examples of a serverless
    networked multiplayer game (peers shared state directly via IP unicast
    and IP multicast, each client simulating independently with latency
    self-correcting over time). Ron Frederick is credited as the author of
    this direct ancestor. See:
        https://github.com/ronf
        https://github.com/ronf/webrtc-spacewar   (MIT License)
        https://www.timeheart.net/spacewar

XSpaceWar-AI is an independent, clean-room implementation. No source code
from the original xspacewar 1.2 distribution is included or copied; the
original C source could not be recovered from any public archive, and the
game's mechanics were reimplemented from their publicly documented history.
Where Ron Frederick's MIT-licensed webrtc-spacewar was consulted as a
reference, our gratitude and attribution are recorded here in accordance
with the MIT License.

Original game concepts, names, and any contributions remain credited to
their respective authors. Nothing in this NOTICE grants rights to any
